result.result:
The owner is entitled to decline the transit of Bab el-Mandeb under the war risks clause of the charter party, and any extra time and bunkers for the alternative route are for the charterers' account. The new route via the Cape of Good Hope adds 4,796.4 nm and 16.0 days, resulting in a new ETA of 2025-02-25T15:00:00Z. VLSFO on board is not sufficient to cover the new route with the required reserve, as there is a shortfall of 22.3 t; therefore, bunkers must be arranged on the way.

The operator should decide whether to confirm the route. If confirmed, the following would follow:
(a) a reply to the owner confirming the route;
(b) an ETA notice to the agent and receiver, as the ETA has moved by 392 hours since the last notice;
(c) a voyage management system entry for the port call ETA in Antwerp.

I recommend that nothing be sent until the operator answers.

